        {
            "id": "bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b:0",
            "title": "Lithium Price Analysis: Carbonate Holds 142,750 Yuan After Recent Pullback",
            "description": "<div class=\"body-bgeA9NCs body-pP5gm7BF content-pP5gm7BF\"><div><span><p class=\"\"><span>Battery material has seen a modest correction in the past session, adding 1,250yuan or 0.88%, as the overall trend leans toward consolidation after a robust first-half rally. Battery-grade </span><a class=\"link-zw5jRdec icon-zw5jRdec\" href=\"https://bravenewcoin.com/insights/lithium-prices-recover-from-july-decline-while-battery-etf-rebounds\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">lithium carbonate</a><span> prices have been volatile as supply and demand fundamentals change across the market.</span></p><p class=\"\"><strong class=\"root-Tkn6WL2y\"><span>Lithium Price Finds Support After Lengthy Pullback</span></strong></p><p class=\"\"><span>The 1-year chart of lithium carbonate illustrates a healthy rebound from late 2025 levels before a correction ensues. Prices increased rapidly in the first few months of 2026 before reaching the levels of almost 200,000 yuan/tonne in May and then easing back to the present 142,750 level.</span></p><figure class=\"container-LTn8RPgW\"><button class=\"previewButton-LTn8RPgW\"><div class=\"preview-ky9wu9YA fixedHeight-ky9wu9YA preview-LTn8RPgW\" style=\"height:inherit;margin:0 auto;max-height:600px;max-width:1117.3814898419864px;aspect-ratio:1.8623024830699775\"><picture class=\"picture-ky9wu9YA\"><source src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-bda0f4da5ebac23ffc8e179b14c5b5b8-resized.webp\" type=\"image/webp\"/><img alt=\"Lithium Price Finds Support After Lengthy Pullback\" class=\"image-ky9wu9YA image-LTn8RPgW\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"presentation\" src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-bda0f4da5ebac23ffc8e179b14c5b5b8-resized.webp\" style=\"background-color:#e4eafb\"/></picture></div></button></figure><p class=\"\"><span>The diagram shows that LIT is finding a higher band than its 2025 lows. Following the May peak, prices retraced through June and July to create a downward trend. The recent advance towards 142,750yuan reflects the market testing a support zone after falling away from the previous rally.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>Today’s daily movement: 0.88% higher as lithium carbonate rebounds from the recent sideways trading sessions. Price has been trading inside a narrow price band near recent lows, indicating lower price volatility relative to the drastic range trading seen earlier in the year.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>The short-term structure has resistance building in the 150,000-160,000 yuan area. Above this zone, it would be a greater correction, whereas if it remains weak, it would be targeted towards a lower support area.</span></p><p class=\"\"><strong class=\"root-Tkn6WL2y\"><span>Lithium Carbonate Technical Indicators Show Neutral Momentum</span></strong></p><p class=\"\"><span>Meanwhile, the TradingView chart for other lithium-related assets appears to have a neutral technical setup. The MACD indicator moved to the middle after previous buying momentum weakened. The latest values read MACD 0.01 and histogram -0.08.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>This is a sign that the momentum is slowing down after the recent push. The directional indicator is not showing a strong directional movement.</span></p><figure class=\"container-LTn8RPgW\"><button class=\"previewButton-LTn8RPgW\"><div class=\"preview-ky9wu9YA fixedHeight-ky9wu9YA preview-LTn8RPgW\" style=\"height:inherit;margin:0 auto;max-height:600px;max-width:984.0954274353876px;aspect-ratio:1.640159045725646\"><picture class=\"picture-ky9wu9YA\"><source src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-2fff54302cc6d64773c8e208f9cdc971-resized.webp\" type=\"image/webp\"/><img alt=\"Lithium Carbonate Technical Indicators Show Neutral Momentum\" class=\"image-ky9wu9YA image-LTn8RPgW\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"presentation\" src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-2fff54302cc6d64773c8e208f9cdc971-resized.webp\" style=\"background-color:#f7f6f7\"/></picture></div></button></figure><p class=\"\"><span>However, the RSI is at about 49.75. The RSI is still at </span><a class=\"link-zw5jRdec\" href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/x/zsA8MIsQ/\" target=\"_blank\">the moderate</a><span> 50 levels and remains somewhat away from its earlier heavy values, signaling that lithium is no longer witnessing the kind of momentum it had witnessed in the previous rally.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>The graph of the lithium stock index displayed another significant intraday move to 242.43. The stock fluctuated primarily between 235 and 238 during the session. The move was enough to take the index away from the recent lows, although momentum indicators showed signs of easing.</span></p><p class=\"\"><strong class=\"root-Tkn6WL2y\"><span>Lithium Market Tracks Supply And Demand Shifts</span></strong></p><p class=\"\"><span>Nonetheless, the lithium carbonate market is still closely following revisions to battery demand, inventory levels, and activity in production. According to market information, lithium prices have recovered from earlier lows and are back up to levels below those seen at the 2026 high earlier this year.</span></p><figure class=\"container-LTn8RPgW\"><button class=\"previewButton-LTn8RPgW\"><div class=\"preview-ky9wu9YA fixedHeight-ky9wu9YA preview-LTn8RPgW\" style=\"height:inherit;margin:0 auto;max-height:600px;max-width:516.162669447341px;aspect-ratio:0.8602711157455684\"><picture class=\"picture-ky9wu9YA\"><source src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-6285f5006e4eb6b54c2c99fe8a1cf8a5-resized.webp\" type=\"image/webp\"/><img alt=\"Lithium Market Tracks Supply And Demand Shifts\" class=\"image-ky9wu9YA image-LTn8RPgW\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"presentation\" src=\"https://s3.tradingview.com/news/image/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b-6285f5006e4eb6b54c2c99fe8a1cf8a5-resized.webp\" style=\"background-color:#7c7c7d\"/></picture></div></button></figure><p class=\"\"><span>Price evaluations conducted over the past three months highlight the continuing vulnerability of battery-grade lithium carbonate to supply responses to demand from the electric vehicle and energy storage markets.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>What is important here, because of the current chart structure, is 142,750 yuan as short-term support. Maintaining this level preserves the recent consolidation scheme; breaking below could carry us down even further.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>On the positive side, lithium carbonate has to return to the 150000 yuan level in order to restore a bullish stance in the short term. Overall, the market is still in the consolidation area between the recovery moves and the correction after the May peak.</span></p></span></div></div>",
            "link": "https://www.tradingview.com/news/bravenewcoin:23cc6f040094b:0/",
            "pub_date": "2026-08-08 20:54:55",
            "source": "Brave New Coin",
            "kind": 1,
            "language": "en"
        },
        {
            "id": "urn:summary_document_report:quartr.com:3688360:0",
            "title": "ANANTRAJ: Q1 FY27 saw 8% revenue growth, higher profits, and strategic moves into cloud and AI services",
            "description": "<div class=\"body-bgeA9NCs body-pP5gm7BF content-pP5gm7BF\"><div class=\"symbolsContainer-rV5QygYP logosContainer-WbDJg_kR\" data-no-swipe=\"true\"></div><div><span><p class=\"\"><span>Consolidated Q1 FY27 revenue rose 8% year-over-year to ₹650.75 crore, with net profit at ₹149.19 crore. Expansion into cloud and AI services, full discharge of NCDs, and a proposed scheme for cloud business restructuring mark key developments.</span></p><p class=\"\"><span>Original document: </span><a class=\"link-zw5jRdec\" href=\"https://www.tradingview.com/accounts/signin?next=https%3A%2F%2Fnews-mediator.tradingview.com%2Fdoc-screener%2Fv1%2Ffiles%2Furn%3Areport%3Aquartr.com%3A3688360-4a94015cd1e71c7142947c92e6a7b541\" target=\"_blank\">Anant Raj Ltd. [ANANTRAJ] Interim report — Aug. 8 2026</a></p><section class=\"variant-secondary-Gmpzg_mv disclaimer-vMD6Mpww\"><b class=\"heading-wrapper-Gmpzg_mv\"><span class=\"heading-Gmpzg_mv\">Disclaimer</span></b><div class=\"content-Gmpzg_mv link-with-underline-Gmpzg_mv\"><span>This is an AI-generated summary and may contain inaccuracies. Please verify any important information with the original source.</span></div></section></span></div></div>",
